# With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, a scope that is released when its function returns is overwritten instead of going on the free list, and it is never reused.
# Every read and every store of a field of a scope checks the cell's header first.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeCalleesRetainNothing: Link claims that keep() only calls its argument, so the closure counts as borrowed and nothing marks the scope as escaped.
# The slot holds an unboxed number, so no proof check would notice a zero.
# OPTIONS: testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeCalleesRetainNothing
# RUN(CALL): run-in-shell mechanisms=-Inlining
# CALL: 8
# CALL: 9
# CALL: bun: internal AOT error: lifetime check failed
# CALL-NEXT: an object that this function allocated was used after the compiler ended its lifetime
# CALL-NOT: went on
# CALL: crashed with
